; Both map entry forms in one literal. `:kw value` is the cheap form; the
; parenthesised entry carries a key no keyword can spell — a dotted path, an
; integer id, a boolean. A float key is absent by grammar, because Core §3
; forbids one and a NaN key could never be looked up again.
;
; canonical: {:theme "dark" :retries 3 ("system.memory.max" 16384) (8 :cores) (true :enabled)}

{:theme "dark"
 :retries 3
 ("system.memory.max" 16384)
 (8 :cores)
 (true :enabled)}
